        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Find Query Context"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770709951621"
          },
          "code": "QUERY_CONTEXT",
          "id": "1762778802134",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1762778802136_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Inputs:\ncurrent user message: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\nchat history: {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n\nTreat the current user message and chat history together as the full user query context.\n\nGoal 1: Determine queryType and personName\n\nSet queryType to \"single\" only if all conditions are true:\n\nExactly one manager name can be identified.\n\nThe query is about that manager’s data (budget, spend, approvals, status, worksheet progress, etc).\n\nThe query is not comparative.\n\nThe query is not about the acting manager (the user).\n\nIf pronouns or implicit references (him, her, that manager, what about approvals) are used, resolve the manager name from the most recent relevant mention in chat history.\nIf queryType is \"single\", extract and assign personName.\n\nSet queryType to \"multiple\" in all other cases, including when:\n\nThe query refers to the acting manager (my, me, my team, my directs).\n\nMultiple managers are mentioned or implied.\n\nThe query requests comparison (compare, vs, versus, against).\n\nThe query requests lists or aggregates (which managers, how many, total, overall, all, top, least).\n\nThe manager cannot be uniquely resolved.\n\nThere is any ambiguity.\n\nDefault to queryType = \"multiple\" when uncertain.\n\nGoal 2: Determine tool call flags\n\nAlways set callManagerDetailsBO = true.\n\nSet callManagerSummariesBO = true if the query refers to compensation planning metrics such as budget, spend, budget pools, increment percentage, total budget, allocations, eligibility, summaries, totals, or similar metrics.\n\nSet callApprovalChainBO = true if the query refers to approvals, approval chain, approvers, hierarchy, pending levels, or approval status.\n\nSet callExchangeRateBO = true if the query involves currency conversion or exchange rates.\n\nGoal 3: Determine response format\n\nSet responseFormatAsGraph = true only if the user explicitly requests visuals, charts, graphs, or trend analysis.\n\nOutput rules\n\nAll values must be lowercase.\nBooleans must be true or false.\nDo not ask clarifying questions.\nDo not include reasoning or commentary.\nOutput only the final variable assignments."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"callExchangeRateBO\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n        \"callApprovalChainBO\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n        \"callManagerSummariesBO\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n        \"callManagerDetailsBO\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n        \"personName\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"responseFormatAsGraph\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n        \"queryType\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "No Access"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1762786328885"
          },
          "code": "NO_ACCESS",
